        body: 'The pharma data analyst category covers several distinct roles: Clinical Data Analyst — analyzes clinical trial data (EDC exports, SDTM datasets) for data quality, trending, and reporting. Typically uses SAS, R, or Python. Pharmacovigilance Data Analyst — analyzes adverse event data for signal detection, PSUR/PBRER analysis, and regulatory compliance reporting. Typically uses Oracle Argus Analytics, Empirica Signal, R, or Python. Biostatistician — designs statistical analyses, performs inferential statistics for efficacy and safety. Requires MS/PhD in biostatistics. Real-World Evidence (RWE) Analyst — analyzes claims, EHR, and registry data for real-world outcomes research. Uses SAS, R, Python, SQL. Quality Data Analyst — analyzes manufacturing batch data, deviation trends, stability data. Uses Excel, Minitab, JMP, or SAS.',
